(*
env: OEVM_NTP_SECONDS=35138
expect:
secs 35138
date nil
finished
*)
(* tuvm#100 (2026-08-01) — ntpDate's STRUCTURAL-NIL path.

   A sync can succeed while no date is available: on the host that is simply
   OEVM_NTP_DATE unset (this test), and on a device it is any boot in which no sync
   has yet completed. The seam answers nil for both, exactly as ntpSyncTz: answers
   one nil for "no network" and "the request timed out" — to a node that will
   free-run either way, the distinction buys nothing and a second failure code
   would force every caller to write a branch it has no different action for.

   Worth testing separately rather than trusting the happy path, because this is
   the branch a correction loop hits FIRST on a cold boot: read the date before the
   first successful sync and you get nil, and a node that writes it to the RTC
   anyway would program the part with garbage. 20_bell/10 proves the value; this
   proves the absence is legible.

   NOTE the pairing with 10_ntp_date.nsl: the two differ by exactly one env line.
   A global export would collapse them into the same test — which is precisely why
   the runner sets env PER TEST (tuvm#88, run_tests_oevm.py). *)
class NtpDateAbsent packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | secs date |
    secs:: platform ntpSyncTz: -25200.
    ('secs ' , secs printString) out.

    date:: platform ntpDate.
    date == nil
      ifTrue:  [ 'date nil' out ]
      ifFalse: [ ('date UNEXPECTED ' , date printString) out ].

    'finished' out.
  )
) : (
)
